        {
          "id": "day2_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h3",
          "text": "Day 2: Monkeys and Bamboo Groves (Wednesday, Nov 6)"
        },
        {
          "id": "day2_morning_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h4",
          "text": "Morning Activity: Arashiyama Bamboo Grove & Tenryu-ji Temple"
        },
        {
          "id": "day2_morning_desc",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Arrive early to experience the ethereal beauty of the bamboo grove with fewer crowds. Afterward, visit the adjacent Tenryu-ji Temple, a UNESCO World Heritage site with a stunning landscape garden that looks beautiful against the backdrop of the Arashiyama mountains."
        },
        {
          "id": "day2_morning_fee",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "caption",
          "text": "Entry Fee: Bamboo Grove is free. Tenryu-ji Temple is approx. ¥500 (garden only)."
        },
        {
          "id": "day2_morning_loc",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "caption",
          "text": "Location: Arashiyama (Western Kyoto). Accessible via JR Saga-Arashiyama Station."
        },
        {
          "id": "day2_divider1",
          "component": "Divider"
        },
        {
          "id": "day2_afternoon_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h4",
          "text": "Afternoon Activity: Iwatayama Monkey Park"
        },
        {
          "id": "day2_afternoon_desc",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "After crossing the scenic Togetsukyo Bridge, embark on a 20-minute uphill hike to this park where Japanese macaques roam freely. The kids will love watching the monkeys, and the panoramic view of Kyoto from the top is a fantastic reward."
        },
        {
          "id": "day2_afternoon_fee",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "caption",
          "text": "Entry Fee: Approx. ¥600 Adult / ¥300 Child."
        },
        {
          "id": "day2_afternoon_loc",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "caption",
          "text": "Location: Arashiyama."
        },
        {
          "id": "day2_divider2",
          "component": "Divider"
        },
        {
          "id": "day2_dinner_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h4",
          "text": "Dinner Suggestion: Arashiyama Casual Dining"
        },
        {
          "id": "day2_dinner_desc",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "While Arashiyama is known for traditional Yudofu (simmered tofu), you can find many family-friendly restaurants near the Togetsukyo Bridge serving tempura, soba noodles, and other popular dishes."
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_card",
          "component": "Card",
          "child": "day3_content"
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_content",
          "component": "Column",
          "children": [
            "day3_title",
            "day3_morning_title",
            "day3_morning_desc",
            "day3_morning_fee",
            "day3_morning_loc",
            "day3_divider1",
            "day3_afternoon_title",
            "day3_afternoon_desc",
            "day3_afternoon_fee",
            "day3_afternoon_loc",
            "day3_divider2",
            "day3_dinner_title",
            "day3_dinner_desc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h3",
          "text": "Day 3: Golden Pavilions and Samurai Action (Thursday, Nov 7)"
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_morning_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h4",
          "text": "Morning Activity: Kinkaku-ji (The Golden Pavilion)"
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_morning_desc",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "One of Kyoto's most famous sights, this Zen temple is covered in gold leaf. The reflection in the surrounding pond is picture-perfect. The route through the grounds is straightforward and doesn't take too long, holding children's attention well."
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_morning_fee",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "caption",
          "text": "Entry Fee: Approx. ¥500."
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_morning_loc",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "caption",
          "text": "Location: Northern Kyoto."
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_divider1",
          "component": "Divider"
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_afternoon_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h4",
          "text": "Afternoon Activity: Toei Kyoto Studio Park (Eigamura)"
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_afternoon_desc",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "A working film set and theme park rolled into one. Explore a replica Edo-period town, watch a live ninja show, try a haunted house, and see samurai movie magic. It's highly interactive and a great contrast to the morning's temple visit."
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_afternoon_fee",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "caption",
          "text": "Entry Fee: Approx. ¥2400 Adult / ¥1200 Child."
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_afternoon_loc",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "caption",
          "text": "Location: Ukyo Ward."
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_divider2",
          "component": "Divider"
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_dinner_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h4",
          "text": "Dinner Suggestion: Okonomiyaki & Yakisoba"
        },
        {
          "id": "day3_dinner_desc",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Find a local restaurant specializing in okonomiyaki (savory pancake) and yakisoba (fried noodles). Kids often enjoy these dishes, especially if you can sit at a counter where the chef cooks on a large griddle in front of you."
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_card",
          "component": "Card",
          "child": "day4_content"
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_content",
          "component": "Column",
          "children": [
            "day4_title",
            "day4_morning_title",
            "day4_morning_desc",
            "day4_morning_fee",
            "day4_morning_loc",
            "day4_divider1",
            "day4_afternoon_title",
            "day4_afternoon_desc",
            "day4_afternoon_fee",
            "day4_afternoon_loc",
            "day4_divider2",
            "day4_dinner_title",
            "day4_dinner_desc"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h3",
          "text": "Day 4: Historic Streets and Market Flavors (Friday, Nov 8)"
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_morning_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h4",
          "text": "Morning Activity: Kiyomizu-dera Temple & Higashiyama Streets"
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_morning_desc",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Visit this magnificent wooden temple perched on a hillside with sweeping views of the city. The walk up to the temple through the historic, preserved streets of Sannenzaka and Ninenzaka is part of the experience, with many small shops and snack stalls."
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_morning_fee",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "caption",
          "text": "Entry Fee: Approx. ¥400."
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_morning_loc",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "caption",
          "text": "Location: Eastern Kyoto."
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_divider1",
          "component": "Divider"
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_afternoon_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h4",
          "text": "Afternoon Activity: Nishiki Market"
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_afternoon_desc",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Known as \"Kyoto's Kitchen,\" this bustling five-block long shopping street is a sensory delight. Let the kids lead the way and try various local snacks on sticks, from mochi and senbei to tako tamago (a tiny octopus with a quail egg in its head)."
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_afternoon_fee",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "caption",
          "text": "Entry Fee: Free to enter; pay for what you eat."
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_afternoon_loc",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "caption",
          "text": "Location: Downtown Kyoto."
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_divider2",
          "component": "Divider"
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_dinner_title",
          "component": "Text",
          "variant": "h4",
          "text": "Dinner Suggestion: Gion District"
        },
        {
          "id": "day4_dinner_desc",
          "component": "Text",
          "text": "Take an early evening stroll through the historic Gion district, Kyoto's famous geisha area. For dinner, find a restaurant serving katsu (breaded and deep-fried pork cutlets) or a family-friendly izakaya for a variety of small dishes."
        },
        {
          "id": "day5_card
